  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 255 AM CDT Mon Aug 10 2026\n\nTuesday...May initially be active if the Monday night-Tue morning \nshortwave and MCS verifies, but after that feature exits the rest of \nTue and Tue night may be mainly dry or at risk for only an isolated \nstorm. Current NBM loaded temps and DPTs are hot and very humid for \nTuesday and easily supportive of heat headlines. But again there is \nmuch uncertainty on convective trends, and cloud debris/storm \noutflow interfering with the ambient temps and how much afternoon \ntime there would be for recovery. Will still message the potential \nbut make heat headline issuance a day by day process for now.\n\nWednesday through Sunday...Medium range ensembles and upper jet \npatterns show the main upper ridge bulge trying to press it's way \neastward acrs the southern plains and low to mid MS RVR Valley mid \nto late week. This process may try to shunt the main storm track \nmore off just to the north of the local area, or if it stalls some \nkeep us in the bullseye of continued daily ring of fire late week \nand even into the weekend. The temperature battle will continue as \nwell with LLVL baroclinicity and thermal ribbon wavering acrs the \nregion for high heat or not so bad depending on the daily flux. Will \nkeep the idea if this pattern holds, there could be quite a bit of \nrainfall build up over the week from the west central plains, acrs \nIA/IL and over to the eastern OH RVR Valley. It's still early, but \ncurrently Thu night looks like a potentail heavy rainfall MCS night \nin the area especially south of I-80.",
